Cough lozenges are dissolvable medicinal products designed to soothe throat irritation and provide symptomatic relief from coughing. Depending on their formulation, they may contain ingredients such as menthol, cough suppressants, herbal extracts, or other compounds intended to ease discomfort.

The market is supported by consumer demand for accessible symptom-relief products and the availability of cough lozenges through pharmacies, supermarkets, and online retailers. Established pharmaceutical brands compete alongside regional manufacturers offering traditional herbal products and affordable alternatives. Growing interest in natural ingredients, convenient dosage forms, and differentiated flavors is influencing product development across the industry.

